    <string name="consent_title">Features and privacy consent</string>
    <string name="consent_feature_title">What this tool does</string>
    <string name="consent_features">· Runs Baidu, Amap and Tencent Location SDKs in order.\n· Each SDK has its own result section.\n· Shows SDK mock location signals:\n  - Baidu: mock probability, anti-mock strategy and distance from the estimated real location.\n  - Amap: isMock and mock location error code 15.\n  - Tencent: isMockGps, fake probability and fake reason.\n· Configure at least one key before checking. SDKs without a key are skipped. Baidu and Amap Android keys require the package name and signing SHA-1; follow Tencent console requirements for its Key.</string>
    <string name="consent_privacy_title">Privacy consent</string>
    <string name="consent_privacy">The three location SDKs collect and process information to provide location checks:\n· Location data: GNSS satellites, cell towers and Wi-Fi information.\n· Network and device data: network type, IP address, Bluetooth, sensors, SIM state, device and system parameters, and identifiers such as OAID, as described in each SDK privacy policy.\n· Tencent also describes anti-fraud monitoring, including identification of malicious, impersonated or tampered applications.\nThe app stores check results and logs on your device. The SDKs may send information to their official services under their privacy policies; the app has no additional upload service.\nTap Agree and continue to accept this notice and the SDK privacy policies. Declining exits the app and disables location checks.</string>
    <string name="consent_links">\nBaidu privacy policy:\nhttps://lbsyun.baidu.com/index.php?title=openprivacy\n\nAmap privacy policy:\nhttps://lbs.amap.com/pages/privacy/\n\nTencent Location SDK privacy policy:\nhttps://privacy.qq.com/document/preview/dbd484ce652c486cb6d7e43ef12cefb0</string>
    <string name="consent_agree">I have read and agree to the features and privacy notice</string>
